\b sb-easy Windows development preview\b0\par\par
This installer adds an automatically started Windows service running as LocalSystem and a lightweight tray that opens local management in your default browser. Administrator permission is required for installation. Open sb-easy normally from the Start menu after setup. The tray starts quietly at sign-in.\par\par
A fresh installation does not enable the VPN. Connections start when requested from the local webpage or according to saved connection settings. TUN connections can change adapters, routes and DNS. Closing the webpage or exiting the tray does not stop the service.\par\par
Close the portable edition and stop its backend before installing. Portable and installed editions use different protected device stores; enroll again in the installed edition.\par\par
Upgrade preserves device data while replacing the old desktop window with local web management. Uninstall stops the connection and removes the service, tray, installed files and shortcuts. Saved device data in ProgramData is retained for reinstall. Use Forget Device in the webpage before uninstall if you want to remove the registration.\par\par
This is an unsigned development preview. Third-party notices are installed with the application. Microsoft Edge WebView2 is not required.\par
